& [Threats]
  + [T01] rewriting historical NotRun is refused by a new profile source UUID and explicit historical-receipt preservation fields
  + [T02] producer self-attestation is refused by an independent Rust verifier over caller-supplied evidence
  + [T03] executable substitution is refused by exact path version bytes and SHA256 constants
  + [T04] stable readOnly laundering is refused by separately retaining its insufficient exact property set
  + [T05] experimental schema name-only claims are refused by exact schema bundle identities and required typed coordinates
  + [T06] profile configuration drift is refused by exact normalized permission entries and network-disabled coordinate
  + [T07] false positive allowed read is refused by exact exit stdout stderr and sentinel hash
  + [T08] false denied read is refused by exact nonzero exit empty stdout Access is denied stderr and forbidden sentinel absence
  + [T09] transcript reordering injection omission or duplicate ids are refused by a closed frame sequence with one explicitly allowed local notification
  + [T10] provider writer MCP Git D-drive or cleanup laundering is refused by zero counters and explicit false gates
  + [T11] path escape symlink reparse and oversized evidence are refused before parse
  + [T12] beta semantics drift is refused by pinned host hash schema hashes and separate future revalidation
  + [T13] App Server service-network overclaim is refused because the receipt claims no packet observation and grants no network authority
  + [T14] Windows enforcement overclaim is refused because the receipt proves only the exact observed commands and preserves unsupported-policy refusal caveats
  + [T15] foreign import is refused by exact staged-path attribution and D-drive read-only policy

& [Residual]
  + command/exec evidence does not prove a full model-driven writer respects the same profile across every tool or approval path
  + the beta profile surface may change in a later host version and must be re-pinned
  + native Windows unsupported split policies can still refuse and WSL remains a separately selectable lane

& [Decision]
  + safe for bounded provider-free capability verification only
